+# Retained public Alpha 8 upgrade
+
+This is the same synthetic account-directory history from reviewed-source ca26ddfc18acb3528969f91289834cdee2d96e69, whose source target was 909977b762ff08f823be1e2c16a4dbb704e4f93a. The next matching public framework/skeleton pair now exists. Preserve the earlier lifecycle plan and source-upgrade report as historical evidence; no new skeleton replaces this application.
+
+Current dependency: public phpthis/framework v0.1.0-alpha.8 through normal Packagist preferred distribution, source/dist 36643c068dda3619f939ac04d861c1316a0af8e9. Matching public skeleton v0.1.0-alpha.8 is 1b1f3afed72880fc7852e67016349e87fc8c4c66. Framework release issue 81 owns the signed tags, artifact verification and clean public create-project evidence.
+
+The installed current contract, knowledge map and upgrade companion are authoritative. Contract 18 / Strict Profile 4 and PHT001-PHT008 remain unchanged from the earlier source checkpoint. The only dependency update is phpthis/framework; the VCS repository override is removed, and PHPStan 2.2.7 / strict-rules 2.0.12 remain locked.
+
+| Boundary | Applicability to this retained public repetition |
+| --- | --- |
+| Contract 14, configuration/request paths | No process configuration input was adopted. Existing literal paths and raw target rejection/preservation tests remain applicable. |
+| Contract 15 / PHT008 | Existing direct constant statements already have distinct named occurrences; policy/order, protected zero-work and one-query list controls remain intact. |
+| Contract 16, source discovery | Existing readable regular PHP/Python files; no application symlink or extensionless entrypoint is adopted. |
+| Contract 17, pending output | Existing single response-emission path and empty/top/lower buffer plus no-fallback tests are retained. |
+| Contract 18, outer HTTP failure | The earlier generic-first front-controller/bootstrap repair is retained. Real built-in-SAPI failure/event/isolation tests remain required; no disclosure inputs or development-details renderer is adopted. |
+| Native PDO construction | The unchanged direct SQLite Connection composition exercises the public native PDO::connect path through the complete consumer tests. SQLite fixture authority and engine evidence remain local only. |
+
+Source, domain operations, SQL, policy, context and tests are preserved except for these targeted dependency/provenance notes. No test, behavior, schema or external service was added or removed. Complete evidence must include strict Composer validation, the entire zero-argument composer check, locked audit, exact installed distribution inventory, a source/test byte comparison and the actual captured runtime. The public repetition is synthetic maintainer evidence; it establishes no independent adoption, live-provider, production, cross-engine, ANN-performance or general productivity claim. The next matching public release remains the lifecycle plan's next maintenance trigger.
